Gragas, Vi, Fizz, Galio, Kayn, Orn, Poppy, Pyke, Riven, Sejuani, Tryndamere, Urgot, Yone, Zac, Renekton, Nidalee, Fiora, Camille

These are travel-time dashes / charges whose damage / crowd-control payload is resolved on arrival and is made more lethal / harder to react to by buffering Flash in the travel to extend / re-angle the arrival and cancel animation. The arrival payload is intrinsic to the dash itself.

Excluded under the stated “landing the dash itself for damage / CC, not reposition only or follow-up only” criterion:
Jarvan E+Q - two-ability set-up, the tech is normally E-Flash to guarantee Q follow-up;
LeBlanc W, Shen E, Rakan W - pure blink / teleport reposition with no travel-time impact payload;
Corki W - no travel dash;
Tristana W - majority view as primarily reposition / escape jump;
Rell W, Bel’Veth Q - no consistent travel-time arrival damage / CC payload used for Flash buffering in common practice.

