2.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: Round 4 locks a 4/5 majority on the travel-time + on-arrival payload definition: Flash buffered mid-travel to extend/re-angle/animation-cancel the dash’s own damage/CC/invul that is resolved on arrival, not pure reposition/escape and not a two-ability set-up.

Majority converged set – Colleagues 1,2,3,5 identical:
Gragas E, Vi Q, Fizz E, Galio E, Kayn Q, Orn E, Poppy E, Pyke E, Riven Q3, Sejuani Q, Tryndamere E, Urgot E, Yone Q3, Zac E, Renekton E, Nidalee W, Fiora Q, Camille E. 
Mechanistic justification retained: undisputed travel charges/dashes with arrival damage/CC – Gragas E, Vi Q, Galio E, Kayn Q, Orn E, Poppy E, Sejuani Q, Urgot E, Zac E, Renekton E, Nidalee W, Fiora Q; stable extensions with same mechanic – Pyke E travel dive with slow/damage on impact, Fizz E travel pass-through with damage/invul kept in window, Camille E Hookshot second stage travel hook with arrival displacement/damage, Riven Q3 chained tumble with arrival damage/knock-up, Yone Q3, Tryndamere E.

Unanimous 17-champion core, Colleague 4 now included:
Gragas, Vi, Fizz, Galio, Kayn, Orn, Poppy, Pyke, Riven, Sejuani, Urgot, Yone, Zac, Renekton, Nidalee, Fiora, Camille. Colleague 4 explicitly aligns with the travel-time + arrival-payload framing, accepts Riven Q3 as legitimate like Yone Q3, and keeps Camille E as limited second-stage hook inclusion. He continues to exclude Jarvan E+Q as follow-up Cataclysm set-up, excludes Shen E as reposition blink, and now explicitly places Tryndamere E outside the core as gap-closer not arrival-payload optimisation.

Stable 5/5 exclusions across Round 4:
Jarvan E+Q – two-ability E into Q/Cataclysm set-up;
LeBlanc W Distortion – pure blink/reposition with follow-up;
Shen E Spectral Walk – pure teleport reposition;
Rakan W Gleam – ally reposition/escape;
Corki W – no dash;
Rell W Queen’s Gambit;
Tristana W Rocket Jump – primarily reposition/escape;
Bel’Veth Q – no consistent travel-time arrival payload consensus.

Remaining disagreement point:
Tryndamere E Spinning Slash – 4/5 keep as travel dash with committed on-arrival damage made more optimal by mid-travel Flash; Colleague 4 frames it as non-payload gap-close/extra range, sitting better outside core.

Colleague 4 evolution from prior rounds:
previously kept Jarvan E+Q, Shen E, doubted Riven/Galio/Kayn/Orn charges; Round 3 moved to accept Riven Q3 and exclude Jarvan E+Q; Round 4 tightens edge to drop Tryndamere E and Shen E while keeping Camille E limited.

Prior belief update:
Kayn Q, Pyke E, Camille E, Fizz E, Riven Q3 remain high-confidence inclusions under majority definition. Jarvan E+Q, Rell W, Tristana W, Bel’Veth Q remain excluded. Core canonical set stable at 17 unanimous, 18 with 4/5 Tryndamere.

Unresolved for next round: final weight of Colleague 4’s Tryndamere E reclassification vs 4/5 arrival-payload reading; whether his acceptance of Riven Q3 and Camille E signals broader convergence toward the 18-champion majority.

